# Flutter Icon Tree-Shake Safety

## Mistake
Release APK build failed because models created icons with `IconData(codePoint, ...)`, which blocks icon tree-shaking.

## Root cause
Persisted `codePoint` values were converted back to icons through non-const `IconData` constructors instead of resolving to compile-time `Icons.*` constants.

## Required recipe
- Persist only `icon.codePoint` in storage.
- Resolve stored code points through a central map of `codePoint -> const Icons.*`.
- Never call `IconData(dynamicValue, fontFamily: 'MaterialIcons')` in app/runtime models.
- Provide a deterministic fallback icon when a code point is missing from the map.

```dart
abstract final class MaterialIconResolver {
  static const fallback = Icons.category_rounded;
  static final _icons = {
    Icons.savings_rounded.codePoint: Icons.savings_rounded,
  };

  static IconData fromCodePoint(int codePoint) => _icons[codePoint] ?? fallback;
}
```

## Regression test pattern
- Add a unit test for resolver known and unknown code points.
- Keep a release-build smoke command in verification: `fvm flutter build apk --release`.
- Audit for forbidden dynamic constructors:
  `rg --no-heading -n "IconData\\(" lib/`.
